Hmm, no reason why you get 139 error. I'll look into this.

> Incidentally, if the code in the setup for map loads a package (with
> library()), there will be an error unless the library call is wrapped in
> suppressPackageStartupMessages(). I guess setup can't produce any output.

This is because RHIPE scans standard error and anything that goes
there is considered an error.
Some packages decide to print to that stream despite no error, and so
RHIPE deems a package load failure.
